"""
A second factor: one-time codes of an authenticator app after RFC 6238,
6 digits every 30 seconds, with HMAC-SHA256 (Standard.Otp) unless the
caller names another hash.  SHA-1, what most apps take when nothing is
said, is offered only through the functions that take a hash, for the
seeds of an older service that used it; the otpauth URI says the hash.

The seed of a user is 20 random bytes, kept in SQLite sealed by
Wolly.Seal under a key of the server and bound to the user name, never in
the clear.  A user turns the factor on in two steps: startEnrolment makes
a seed and gives it out once, for the app; confirmEnrolment turns it on
when a code of the app fits.  Until then the login asks for no code.

A code fits when it is the code of the step of now or of the step before
or after, for a clock that is off by up to 30 seconds.  A step that was
taken once is not taken again, nor any step before it: a code seen over
a shoulder or in a log opens nothing after it was used.  Counting and
refusing too many tries is Wolly.Auth's, which calls checkCode.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String,
    length
);
import Standard.Otp (
    OtpHash
);
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);

module Wolly.Totp is
    """
    The seconds of one step: 30.
    """
    function stepSeconds(): Int64
        ensures result = 30;

    """
    The digits of a code: 6.
    """
    function codeDigits(): Index
        ensures result = 6;

    """
    Makes the table of seeds, if it is not there.  None when it exists
    afterwards.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function prepareTotp(db: &![Database[Writing], R]): Option[DbError];

    """
    Whether the second factor of name is on.  Right false for a name
    without a seed or with one not yet confirmed.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function totpEnabled(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N]): Either[DbError, Bool];

    """
    A new seed for name, sealed under key and kept, not yet on; a seed of
    an earlier start that was never confirmed is replaced.  Right Some
    holds the seed in base32 without padding, for the app and nowhere
    else.  Right None when the factor of name is on already or the random
    source or the seal failed.  name is taken as it is: the caller passes
    the user of a session, never a name from a request.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database and of the random source.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, N: Region]
    function startEnrolment(db: &![Database[Writing], R], key: Span[Nat8, K], name: Span[Nat8, N]): Either[DbError, Option[String]];

    """
    Turns the factor of name on when code fits the seed of its start at
    now.  Right false when there is no started seed, the factor is on
    already, or code does not fit; the step of the code counts as taken.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, N: Region, C: Region]
    function confirmEnrolment(db: &![Database[Writing], R], key: Span[Nat8, K], name: Span[Nat8, N],
        code: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64): Either[DbError, Bool]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    Whether code is a code of name at now: the factor is on, code is
    codeDigits digits and the code of the step of now, the step before or
    the step after, and that step is later than every step taken before.
    Right true takes the step.  Right false otherwise, also when the seed
    does not open under key.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, N: Region, C: Region]
    function checkCode(db: &![Database[Writing], R], key: Span[Nat8, K], name: Span[Nat8, N], code: Span[Nat8, C],
        now: Int64): Either[DbError, Bool]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    As confirmEnrolment, with the codes made by hash.
    No ensures: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, N: Region, C: Region]
    function confirmEnrolmentWith(db: &![Database[Writing], R], key: Span[Nat8, K], name: Span[Nat8, N],
        code: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64, hash: OtpHash): Either[DbError, Bool]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    As checkCode, with the codes made by hash.
    No ensures: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, N: Region, C: Region]
    function checkCodeWith(db: &![Database[Writing], R], key: Span[Nat8, K], name: Span[Nat8, N], code: Span[Nat8, C],
        now: Int64, hash: OtpHash): Either[DbError, Bool]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    Removes the seed of name, on or not.  Right true when there was one.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function removeTotp(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N]): Either[DbError, Bool];

    """
    The otpauth URI of the seed secret, in base32 as startEnrolment gave
    it, for the account name at issuer: what the app reads from a QR code.
    """
    generic [I: Region, N: Region, S: Region]
    function otpauthFor(issuer: Span[Nat8, I], name: Span[Nat8, N], secret: Span[Nat8, S]): String
        ensures length(&result) > 0;

    """
    As otpauthFor, with the URI naming hash as its algorithm.
    No contract: its length follows the input.
    """
    generic [I: Region, N: Region, S: Region]
    function otpauthWith(issuer: Span[Nat8, I], name: Span[Nat8, N], secret: Span[Nat8, S], hash: OtpHash): String;
end module.
